/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 44 0 R
/T (Perhaps one of the best examples of Iranian ingenuity under sanctions pressure is the Shahed 149, called Gaza. On the spec sheet, it is a direct competitor to the American MQ series, and at home, it is often projected as such. Powered by a turboprop engine like the Shahed 147, it is capable of flying at tremendous heights, up to 35,000 feet. Although it is significantly lower than the Shahed 147's claimed 60,000 feet, the Gaza makes up for it by being armed to the teeth with small guided missiles and bombs that are capable of engaging both hardened and soft targets .)
/E (Perhaps one of the best examples of Iranian ingenuity under sanctions pressure is the Shahed 149, called Gaza. On the spec sheet, it is a direct competitor to the American MQ series, and at home, it is often projected as such. Powered by a turboprop engine like the Shahed 147, it is capable of flying at tremendous heights, up to 35,000 feet. Although it is significantly lower than the Shahed 147's claimed 60,000 feet, the Gaza makes up for it by being armed to the teeth with small guided missiles and bombs that are capable of engaging both hardened and soft targets .)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [58]
>>
endobj
